Z||000009||ur2biteme||02-07-2001||01:42 AM||||my car had the same problem as this one.  the lights would go up but not down.  check to see if the instrument cluster lights and all the other running lights work too when he flips the switch.  turns out one of the positive leads was shorting out on the frame of the radio.  insulated the wire, changed the fuse and the lights went back down.  thought you'd might like to know. hope it helps.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>aproaching 171k :)<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>a little piece of my madness</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||MontanaFiero||02-07-2001||03:14 AM||||Headlamps-- also could just be a bad switch or loose connector on the back of the switch... when you turn the lights off, it actually turns the motors "on" to wind down the lights. There is a relay involved, but cheap and easy fix.||||reg||1
